  "problem": "The price of crude oil, measured in dollars per barrel, increases at a rate $r(t)$ given by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\frac{2}{1+3t},\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in dollars per month, and $t>0$ is the time in months since the start of a particular year.\n\nIf the price was $$25$ per barrel at the start of the year, which expression gives the price of crude oil $t$ months since the start of the year?",
